Treasury Regulation Sections <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">1.897-2(h)</FONT> and <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">1.1445-2(c)(3),</FONT> including the required notice to the U.S. Internal Revenue Service, stating that an interest in Blocker is
not a &#147;United States real property interest&#148; within the meaning of Section&nbsp;897(c) of the Code. </P></TD></TR></TABLE> <P STYLE="margin-top:18pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><B><I>Bridger Parties and
Blocker Conditions to Closing </I></B></P> <P STYLE="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">The obligation of the Bridger Parties and Blocker to consummate or cause to be consummated the
Transactions is subject to the satisfaction of the following additional conditions, any one or more of which may be waived in writing by Bridger. </P> <P STYLE="font-size:6pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt">&nbsp;</P>
<TABLE STYLE="BORDER-COLLAPSE:COLLAPSE; font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:10pt" BORDER="0" CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" WIDTH="100%">
